## 3. Content that is *not* in the SRD

The catalogs also cover material that is **not** part of SRD 5.2.1 — entries restated from
the 2024 rulebooks and from setting sourcebooks. That material is not ours and never was.
The MIT license in `LICENSE` covers the code that *describes* these rules; it grants no
rights in the underlying game content, because there are none of ours to grant. The
restatements are unofficial and fan-made.

- **Species** — Tortle, Fairy, Bugbear, Aasimar.
  (SRD 5.2.1 species are Dragonborn, Dwarf, Elf, Gnome, Goliath, Halfling, Human,
  Orc, and Tiefling.)
- **Subclasses** — College of Glamour (Bard), Light Domain (Cleric), Circle of the Moon
  (Druid), Assassin (Rogue), Phantom (Rogue), Great Old One Patron (Warlock).
  (SRD 5.2.1 carries exactly one subclass per class: Path of the Berserker, College of
  Lore, Life Domain, Circle of the Land, Champion, Warrior of the Open Hand, Oath of
  Devotion, Hunter, Thief, Draconic Sorcery, Fiend Patron, and Evoker.)
- **Class features** — Cunning Strike and its rider options.
- **Backgrounds** — Entertainer, Farmer, Genie Touched, Marked Wanderer, and the one-off
  backgrounds declared via `background.custom` in the example characters. (SRD 5.2.1
  backgrounds are Acolyte, Criminal, Sage, and Soldier.)
- **Campaign-setting content** — `background.marked-wanderer` is an Exandria background
  (Critical Role, *Explorer's Guide to Wildemount*). `spell.spellfire-flare` is a Forgotten
  Realms spell, from *Forgotten Realms: Heroes of Faerûn*. Neither setting's material is
  covered by the CC-BY-4.0 grant above.
- Assorted spells, feats, magic items, and Eldritch Invocations beyond the SRD lists —
  among the magic items, `item.sentinel-shield` restates a Dungeon Master's Guide entry.
- **Homebrew** — `item.ring-of-comprehension` restates no published item. It is the Helm
  of Comprehending Languages reworked as a charged ring, for one campaign.

If you intend to redistribute this project or build on it commercially, review these
entries first: the MIT grant on the code carries no rights in the rules they describe.

## 4. Third-party software and fonts

Nothing in this section is vendored into the repository or the published package.

- **`@preview/cuti`** is a compile-time dependency (`src/layout/common.typ`), used for its
  synthesized bold and small-caps helpers. It is resolved from the Typst package registry
  and is licensed under the MIT License.
- **ETBembo** (MIT), **Montserrat** (OFL 1.1), and **Euler Math** (OFL 1.1) are the three
  fonts the layout is calibrated to. The Nix flake takes them from nixpkgs; a non-Nix build
  resolves them from the host. No font file is distributed with this package.

